## 2) Aisency vs This CRM for Bulk WhatsApp Messages

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Answer: YES — your CRM already supports bulk WhatsApp messaging and can replace Aisency for broadcast campaigns.**

### What Your CRM Already Does (No Extra Service Needed)
Your CRM at `frontend-liart-gamma-68.vercel.app` already has:

| Feature | Your CRM | Aisency |
|---|---|---|
| **Bulk WhatsApp Broadcast** | ✅ Built-in via Meta Cloud API (Broadcasts page) | ✅ Paid service |
| **CSV Upload & Map** | ✅ Upload CSV → map columns → send | ✅ Similar |
| **Meta Approved Templates** | ✅ Synced from Meta Business Manager | ✅ Uses own templates |
| **Schedule Broadcasts** | ✅ Schedule for future date/time | ✅ Yes |
| **Media Attachments** | ✅ Image/Video/Document/Template | ✅ Yes |
| **Delivery Logs** | ✅ Webhook event tracking | ✅ Yes |
| **Meta Lead Ads Integration** | ✅ Verified | ❌ Separate setup |
| **Cost** | **Free** (you pay Meta API costs only) | **Paid subscription** |

### Recommendation
- **Stop paying Aisency** for WhatsApp broadcast if you're only using it for bulk template messages.
- Your CRM sends messages directly via Meta Cloud API using your own WhatsApp Business number (+91 9175635165).
- The only cost is Meta's per-conversation pricing (~₹0.50/business-initiated conversation).
- For Meta Ads lead capture, your CRM already has webhook-based lead ingestion.

> [!WARNING]
> **One limitation**: Aisency may offer advanced features like chatbot flow builders, auto-replies with AI, or multi-agent inbox. Your CRM has FAQ Bot and AI Assistant pages, but they need backend configuration. If you need those advanced automation features, keep Aisency for chatbot automation only and use your CRM for broadcasts.

